  "content": {
    "id": "p3-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "A fair four-sided die is labelled with the numbers 1, 2, 3 and 4. The die is rolled and the result is recorded.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p3-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Write down the sample space.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\Omega=\\{1,2,3,4\\}$.",
          "worked": "The possible recorded results are the four face labels, so $\\Omega=\\{1,2,3,4\\}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p3-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "There are sixteen events for this experiment. Write down all of these.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\varnothing$;\n\n$\\{1\\},\\{2\\},\\{3\\},\\{4\\}$;\n\n$\\{1,2\\},\\{1,3\\},\\{1,4\\},\\{2,3\\},\\{2,4\\},\\{3,4\\}$;\n\n$\\{1,2,3\\},\\{1,2,4\\},\\{1,3,4\\},\\{2,3,4\\}$;\n\n$\\{1,2,3,4\\}$.",
          "worked": "Each event is a subset of $\\Omega$. Listing subsets by their number of elements gives:\n\nNo elements: $\\varnothing$.\n\nOne element: $\\{1\\},\\{2\\},\\{3\\},\\{4\\}$.\n\nTwo elements: $\\{1,2\\},\\{1,3\\},\\{1,4\\},\\{2,3\\},\\{2,4\\},\\{3,4\\}$.\n\nThree elements: $\\{1,2,3\\},\\{1,2,4\\},\\{1,3,4\\},\\{2,3,4\\}$.\n\nFour elements: $\\{1,2,3,4\\}$.\n\nThere are $1+4+6+4+1=16$ events.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p3-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the probability corresponding to each of these events.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\Pr(\\varnothing)=0$.\n\n$\\Pr(\\{1\\})=\\Pr(\\{2\\})=\\Pr(\\{3\\})=\\Pr(\\{4\\})=\\frac14$.\n\n$\\Pr(\\{1,2\\})=\\Pr(\\{1,3\\})=\\Pr(\\{1,4\\})=\\frac12$.\n\n$\\Pr(\\{2,3\\})=\\Pr(\\{2,4\\})=\\Pr(\\{3,4\\})=\\frac12$.\n\n$\\Pr(\\{1,2,3\\})=\\Pr(\\{1,2,4\\})=\\frac34$.\n\n$\\Pr(\\{1,3,4\\})=\\Pr(\\{2,3,4\\})=\\frac34$.\n\n$\\Pr(\\{1,2,3,4\\})=1$.",
          "worked": "The four outcomes are equally likely. For each event $E$,\n\n$$\\Pr(E)=\\frac{n(E)}{4}.$$\n\nThus:\n\n$\\Pr(\\varnothing)=0$.\n\n$\\Pr(\\{1\\})=\\Pr(\\{2\\})=\\Pr(\\{3\\})=\\Pr(\\{4\\})=\\frac14$.\n\n$\\Pr(\\{1,2\\})=\\Pr(\\{1,3\\})=\\Pr(\\{1,4\\})=\\frac24=\\frac12$.\n\n$\\Pr(\\{2,3\\})=\\Pr(\\{2,4\\})=\\Pr(\\{3,4\\})=\\frac24=\\frac12$.\n\n$\\Pr(\\{1,2,3\\})=\\Pr(\\{1,2,4\\})=\\frac34$.\n\n$\\Pr(\\{1,3,4\\})=\\Pr(\\{2,3,4\\})=\\frac34$.\n\n$\\Pr(\\{1,2,3,4\\})=\\frac44=1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
    ]
  },
